# Skill: SSH to a server

Use the helper `scripts/ssh_run.sh` to open an interactive SSH session or run a
one-off command on a remote host. Prefer it over hand-writing `ssh` lines so
connection options (port, identity, jump host, timeouts) stay consistent.

## How to run

```bash
# Interactive login shell
scripts/ssh_run.sh -H <user>@<host>

# Run a single remote command (everything after `--` runs on the server)
scripts/ssh_run.sh -H <host> -u <user> -i <key> -- '<remote command>'
```

Key options: `-H/--host`, `-u/--user`, `-p/--port` (default 22),
`-i/--identity <key>`, `-J/--jump <bastion>`, `-t` (force TTY),
`-o KEY=VALUE` (extra `ssh -o` option, repeatable), `--dry-run`.

Defaults can come from env vars: `SSH_HOST`, `SSH_USER`, `SSH_PORT`, `SSH_IDENTITY`.

## Agent guidance

- **Confirm the host before connecting** if it was not given explicitly; never
  invent a hostname or IP.
- Always check the exact command with `--dry-run` first when the remote command
  is destructive (writes, deletes, deploys).
- Quote the remote command as a single argument after `--` so local shell
  expansion does not apply to remote variables/globs.
- For an unreachable host, report the error; do not retry blindly or disable
  host-key checking unless the user explicitly asks.
- Chain remote steps with `&&` inside one quoted command to avoid repeated
  logins, e.g. `-- 'cd /work && ./build-tools/build.sh -o ./build'`.

## Examples

```bash
scripts/ssh_run.sh -H dev@10.0.0.5 -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 -- 'nvidia-smi; npu-smi info'
scripts/ssh_run.sh -H target -J bastion.example.com -- 'cd /work && git pull'
SSH_HOST=dev@10.0.0.5 scripts/ssh_run.sh -- 'uname -a'
```
